    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="0622" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg588"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April 15,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1400.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your examination and
                    report copy of a letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d611-f1"/> from Messrs. Seropian
                    Brothers, brokers and commission merchants at Fresno, Cal., relative to
                    information that has reached them that they are to be deprived of certain real
                    estate in Marsovan on the ground that “no citizen of the United States has a
                    right to inherit or own real estate in Turkey.”</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
